{"id":"86e049e41efbbcc9","group":"93","path":"93/93-lem-filter-intersection.md","title":"Filter Intersection","display":"Filter Intersection","type":"lemma","metadata":{"type":"lemma","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-lem-filter-intersection","aliases":["93-lem-filter-intersection"],"display":"Filter Intersection","authors":"W. J. Blok, Don Pigozzi","book_title":"Algebraizable Logics","depends_on":["[[93-df-filter]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"lemma"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-lem-filter-intersection"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-lem-filter-intersection</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"Filter Intersection"},{"key":"authors","html":"W. J. Blok, Don Pigozzi"},{"key":"book_title","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"9beeac4373d773f8\" href=\"?note=9beeac4373d773f8\" title=\"93-df-filter\">93-df-filter</a></span></div>"}],"html":"<h1 id=\"lem-filter-intersection---Filter-Intersection\">lem-filter-intersection - Filter Intersection</h1>\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I\\in V\">\\(I\\in V\\)</span> with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I\\ne\\varnothing\">\\(I\\ne\\varnothing\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F:I\\to V\">\\(F:I\\to V\\)</span>, every <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F(i)\">\\(F(i)\\)</span> is in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Fil}(\\mathbf A)\">\\(\\mathrm{Fil}(\\mathbf A)\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\bigcap\\operatorname{ran}(F)\\ne\\varnothing\">\\(\\bigcap\\operatorname{ran}(F)\\ne\\varnothing\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Fil}(\\mathbf A)\">\\(\\mathrm{Fil}(\\mathbf A)\\)</span> is the filter family of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"9beeac4373d773f8\" href=\"?note=9beeac4373d773f8\" title=\"93-df-filter\">93-df-filter</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"I\\in V\\land I\\ne\\varnothing\\land F:I\\to V\n\\land\\forall i\\in I\\;\\bigl(F(i)\\in\\mathrm{Fil}(\\mathbf A)\\bigr)\n\\land\\bigcap\\operatorname{ran}(F)\\ne\\varnothing\n\\to\\bigcap\\operatorname{ran}(F)\\in\\mathrm{Fil}(\\mathbf A).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[I\\in V\\land I\\ne\\varnothing\\land F:I\\to V\n\\land\\forall i\\in I\\;\\bigl(F(i)\\in\\mathrm{Fil}(\\mathbf A)\\bigr)\n\\land\\bigcap\\operatorname{ran}(F)\\ne\\varnothing\n\\to\\bigcap\\operatorname{ran}(F)\\in\\mathrm{Fil}(\\mathbf A).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>An intersection of lattice filters is meet-closed and upward closed; the displayed nonemptiness clause is necessary for unbounded lattices. It is automatic when the lattice has a greatest element.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"lem-filter-intersection---Filter-Intersection","text":"lem-filter-intersection - Filter Intersection","level":1},{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-filter","status":"resolved","id":"9beeac4373d773f8","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-filter]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-filter","status":"resolved","id":"9beeac4373d773f8","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Fil}(\\mathbf A)$ is the filter family of [[93-df-filter]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"I\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"I\\ne\\varnothing","display":false},{"tex":"F:I\\to V","display":false},{"tex":"F(i)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Fil}(\\mathbf A)","display":false},{"tex":"\\bigcap\\operatorname{ran}(F)\\ne\\varnothing","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Fil}(\\mathbf A)","display":false},{"tex":"I\\in V\\land I\\ne\\varnothing\\land F:I\\to V\n\\land\\forall i\\in I\\;\\bigl(F(i)\\in\\mathrm{Fil}(\\mathbf A)\\bigr)\n\\land\\bigcap\\operatorname{ran}(F)\\ne\\varnothing\n\\to\\bigcap\\operatorname{ran}(F)\\in\\mathrm{Fil}(\\mathbf A).","display":true}],"bytes":1005,"backlinks":[],"outgoing":["9beeac4373d773f8"]}